      "description": "UCM Career Opportunities | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Cook- Part Time | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Cook- Part Time | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. UCM Career Opportunities Menu UCM Career Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Cook- Part Time Print Apply ﻿ Cook- Part Time Salary $15.00 Hourly Location Child Care Center - Foster/Knox Building, MO Job Type Non-Exempt Staff Part Time Job Number 999348 Division Foster Knox Child Care Opening Date 09/02/2026 Description Benefits Questions Description Devise and update weekly menus and shopping lists.  Purchase food weekly.  Prepares and serves meals for the children at the Child Care Centers. Maintains complete and accurate records of food purchased and prepared. Child Care Centers Foster-Knox provides child care services to the University and the Warrensburg community. Examples of Duties Prepare and serve breakfast and lunch following established menu, serving sizes and times.  Review and revise current recipes for bulk food production.  Create weekly menus and shopping lists. 45% Organize and/or prepare snacks following established menu, serving sizes and times. 15% Establish a routine that enables baked goods to be prepared in advance. 15% Maintain complete, accurate records of weekly food purchases and food production forms daily. 8% Analyze and develop menus and shopping lists to be cost-effective. Purchase local food items and supplies from established shopping lists; may substitute for seasonal or special-priced items. Inventory and request purchases from a university-contracted food source or service. 12% Oversee proper maintenance of the kitchen and kitchen supplies.  Assure all food storage and preparation areas are completed in a safe, clean and sanitary manner.  Assist with laundry duties when needed. 5% Typical Qualifications Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Experience: Minimum of six (6) months’ experience in food preparation/cooking. Nutrition background/training preferred. Supplemental Information Lead worker: assigns, trains, schedules, oversees, or reviews the work of others. 10% 1-3 Stuend employees, including a Graduate Assistant. 10% This position requires: Post-Offer Physical Exam Required, within 30 days of employment Fingerpringing Child Care Security Check- Family Care Safety Registration completed after fingerprinting Valid US driver's license TB Screening as required by licensing CPR and First Aid within the first 90 days of employment: must be pediatric CPR Working Hours and Day: Morning hours Monday through Friday, equal 25 hours a week (7:00am - 12:00pm) The earliest anticipated start date for this position is November 16, 2026. Special Instructions: Full-time staff & 12-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks paid vacation per year; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. 9-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. Part-time benefits-eligible positions: Benefits include generous education assistance for the employee. Temporary, adjunct, student employment, or graduate assistant positions: Benefits are not included. Completed UCM online application for employment required. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A review will begin immediately and continue until filled unless indicated otherwise. NOTE: A background check is required for the selected candidate of all staff, faculty, adjunct, and temporary positions and any job offer is contingent on the results of this check. Student employees and graduate assistants do not require a background check to be conducted prior to employment. The University of Central Missouri is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our faculty and staff are the university’s most valuable asset, and our goal is to provide a robust Total Rewards Program designed to help them maintain a happy, healthy, and productive lifestyle. Highlights from UCM's total rewards package for full-time employees include: 32% (staff) and 6% (faculty) defined retirement contribution, paid 100% by the university; Voluntary Tax-Sheltered Annuity (TSA) programs (403(b) and 457(b)) that allow eligible employees to make additional pre-tax contributions to a retirement plan; Employees can earn up to 6 credit hours for themselves per academic year. Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans that begin on the first of the month following your date of hire. Basic dental and vision insurance paid at 100% by the university; Available Health and Dependent Flexible Spending Accounts; University-paid basic life insurance (including accidental death and dismemberment) and short-term and long-term disability insurance coverage; Generous leave accruals that begin accruing on your start date, plus 14 paid holidays per year. The UCM Childcare Center on the Warrensburg campus can provide faculty, staff, and students quality care for their children ages six weeks to 10 years. The Student Recreation and Wellness Center (SRWC) is free for all employees and is located on the Warrensburg campus. An Employee Assistance Program is available to all employees and their immediate family members to help assist with personal challenges you may face in your daily life; UCM offers an Employee Discount Program through Working Advantage. To learn more about the wonderful benefits available as a University of Central Missouri employee, visit our benefits page ! 01 Do you have a valid US driver's license? Yes No 02 Do you have a High School diploma or GED? Yes No 03 Do you have a minimum of 6 months' experience in food preparation/cooking? Yes No Required Question Employer University of Central Missouri (UCM) Address PO Box 800 Warrensburg, Missouri, 64093-5299 Phone (660) 543-4255 Website https://www.ucmo.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email UCM Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Se