    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ucmo/jobs/5465782/multimedia-specialist": {
      "title": "Multimedia Specialist",
      "description": "UCM Career Opportunities | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Multimedia Specialist | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Multimedia Specialist | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. UCM Career Opportunities Menu UCM Career Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Multimedia Specialist Print Apply ﻿ Multimedia Specialist Salary $53,521.00 Annually Location UCMO - Warrensburg, MO Job Type Exempt Staff Full Time Job Number 999507 Division IT Service Management Opening Date 08/28/2026 Description Benefits Questions Description Under the general lead of the Coordinator of Multimedia Technologies, the Multimedia Specialist is responsible for providing multimedia related services to over 300 classrooms, and some 100 conference rooms and other venues across 60 buildings on the UCM Campus. The position also supports the University's well-established online learning program. More specifically, the position will: Install and support audio/visual and classroom technologies; Provide consultation for deployment projects and other multimedia related efforts; Train end-users on the use of multimedia technology and control systems; Prepare and maintain documentation. Examples of Duties Managing and expanding audio/visual operational activities: - 70% Install, configure, support and troubleshoot audio/video components including but not limited to, speakers, microphones, cameras, projectors, signal management/monitoring gear and SIP /VoIP collaboration endpoints and all infrastructure components Support of Christie, Crestron, Cisco, commercial/event/learning A/V products and SIP /IP interactive technologies; Implementing and administrating common audio/visual and interactive TCP /IP and HDBaseT-based services, including HDMI , VGA , DHCP , HTTP , etc.; Proactively develop strategies to promptly resolve issues regarding infrastructure health and operational readiness; Identify, research, and propose new technologies, services, and/or products to enhance the functionality, and/or cost effectiveness; Perform monitoring/analysis on operating system functionality and use tools associated with audio/video quality/performance and network performance. Leading, guiding and developing audio-visual technology-related projects and services: - 20% Collaborate with senior level university stakeholders and vendors on projects and university/division-wide initiatives; Manage operational area projects including: Completion of standard project plan documentation: Development and management of project schedule and resources; and, Regular project status reporting regarding schedule, budget, and expected results. Work independently and with team members to improve the university AV infrastructure and enterprise systems in order to provide maximum performance and reliability. Maintaining an accurate inventory and documentation of all UCM -owned technology devices and software: - 10% Develop and establish audio/video and interactive infrastructure standards and procedures. Revise and/or develop university audio/visual processes/procedures for the effective and proper usage of technologies; Ensure thorough research, development, and communication regarding the introduction of new equipment, software or services; Typical Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Technology, Educational Technology, Instructional Technology or related field required. Education may be substituted for experience or experience may be substituted for education based on the following: AA = 2 years experience; BA/BS = 4 years experience; MA/MS = 6 years experience. Experience: Two years’ experience in a technical environment required. One year experience with multimedia or audio-visual systems preferred. Supplemental Information Physical/Environmental Factors: Lifting (weight) - 50 lbs Please note that the University of Central Missouri does not provide immigration sponsorship or support (e.g., H-1B, F-1 OPT, TN visa sponsorship) for employees in this role.  All applicants must possess valid US work authorization at the time of hire. This role requires full-time, on-site work at our Warrensburg, Missouri campus and is not eligible for full-time remote work. The selected candidate will be required to work on-site in Warrensburg, Missouri each day. Special Instructions: Full-time staff & 12-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks paid vacation per year; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. 9-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. Part-time benefits-eligible positions: Benefits include generous education assistance for the employee. Temporary, adjunct, student employment, or graduate assistant positions: Benefits are not included. Completed UCM online application for employment required. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A review will begin immediately and continue until filled unless indicated otherwise. NOTE: A background check is required for the selected candidate of all staff, faculty, adjunct, and temporary positions and any job offer is contingent on the results of this check. Student employees and graduate assistants do not require a background check to be conducted prior to employment. The University of Central Missouri is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our faculty and staff are the university’s most valuable asset, and our goal is to provide a robust Total Rewards Program designed to help them maintain a happy, healthy, and productive lifestyle. Highlights from UCM's total rewards package for full-time employees include: 32% (staff) and 6% (faculty) defined retirement contribution, paid by the university; Voluntary Tax-Sheltered Annuity (TSA) programs (403(b) and 457(b)) that allow eligible employees to make additional pre-tax contributions to a retirement plan; Employees can earn up to full tuition (15 credit hours) for themselves per academic year. Full-time employees are also eligible for up to $175 towards non-credit courses each fiscal year. Employees can earn up to full tuition for their dependents; Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans that begin on the first of the month following your date of hire. Basic dental and vision insurance paid at 100% by the university; Available Health and Dependent Flexible Spending Accounts; University-paid basic life insurance (including accidental death and dismemberment) and short-term and long-term disability insurance coverage; Generous leave accruals that begin accruing on your start date, plus 14 paid holidays per year. The UCM Childcare Center on the Warrensburg campus can provide faculty, staff, and students quality care for their children ages six weeks to 10 years. The Student Recreation and Wellness Center (SRWC) is free for all employees and is located on the Warrensburg campus. An Employee Assistance Program is available to all employees and their immediate family members to help assist with personal challenges you may face in your daily life; UCM offers an Employee Discount Program through Working Advantage. To learn more about the wonderful benefits available as a University of Central Missouri employee, visit our benefits page ! 01 Will you now or in the future require employer sponsorship to acquire or maintain U.S. work authorization? This would include items such as OPT, CPT, H-1B, or employer-sponsored permanent residency. Yes No 02 This role requires full-time, on-site work at our Warrensburg, Missouri campus and is not eligible for full-time remote work. Are you able to work on-site in Warrensburg, Missouri each day? Yes, I am able to work on-site in Warrensburg, Missouri each day, as required, and understand that this role requires full-time, on-campus presence. This position is not a remote position. No, I am looking for a remote position, and I am unable to report to on-site work in Warrensburg, Missouri, each day, as expected. 03 Which statement below best describes the highest level of education you have completed? High school graduate, diploma or the equivalent (GED) Associate degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Professional degree Doctorate degree 04 How many years of experience in a technical environment do you currently have? No experience. Less than 1 year of experience. More than 1 year, but less than 2 years of experience. More than 2 years, but less than 3 years of experience. More than 3 years, but less than 4 years of experience. More than 4 years, but less than 5 years of experience. More than 5 years of experience. 05 I understand that, as a condition of employment for this position, I am required to complete a criminal background check and obtain Criminal Justice Information Security (CJIS) clearance, which includes a fingerprint-based criminal history check. Yes, I understand that, prior to being offered this position, I am required to successfully obtain Criminal Justice Information Security (CJIS) clearance through a fingerprint-based criminal history check, in addition to completing a criminal background check. 06 Please explain your experience in a technical environment in great detail. 07 Do you currently have valid US work authorization that permits you to work for University of Central Missouri? Yes No 08 Will you require University of Central Missouri’s sponsorship or support (e.g., H-1B, F-1 OPT, TN visa sponsorship) to acquire and maintain valid US work authorization in the future? Yes No 09 If you answered \"Yes\" to the previous question, please explain. Required Question Employer University of Central Missouri (UCM) Address PO Box 800 Warrensburg, Missouri, 64093-5299 Phone (660) 543-4255 Website https://www.ucmo.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email UCM Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this set