      "description": "UCM Career Opportunities | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Career Advisor Consultant | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Career Advisor Consultant | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. UCM Career Opportunities Menu UCM Career Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Career Advisor Consultant Print Apply ﻿ Career Advisor Consultant Salary $50,000.00 Annually Location UCMO - Warrensburg, MO Job Type Exempt Staff Full Time Job Number 999762 Division Regional Prof. Development Center Opening Date 08/21/2026 Description Benefits Description To equip educators with resources that support every Missouri student in developing a clear, personalized path to success through comprehensive career exploration and real-world learning experiences. A Missouri Regional Career Advisor (RCA) is a strategic partner, educator, coach, and system navigator who strengthens career development efforts across districts while helping ensure every Missouri student is success-ready upon graduation. RCAs model the knowledge, skills, and dispositions that drive high-quality This position will support schools in the Kansas City Region Examples of Duties 100% - Career Advising to include: Missouri Connections Provide training, technical assistance, guidance, and best practices to support effective integration of Missouri Connections. Participate in ongoing training to stay current on platform updates and enhancements. ICAP (Individual Career and Academic Plan) Support district and area career center staff in implementing a comprehensive, relevant, and student-centered ICAP process. Student-Centered Events Partner with districts to plan and support career-connected learning experiences, including STEAM and career-focused events. PLANNING/COMMUNICATION/COLLABORATION ACTIVITIES Career Advisors will: Coordinate and facilitate regional Missouri Connections trainings in alignment with DESE expectations and approval processes. Deliver in-person and virtual trainings approved by DESE School Counseling staff. Communicate and obtain approval for any additional training requests. Ensure all conference presentations are approved prior to submission or delivery. Collaborate closely with the Missouri Connections State Trainer to remain current on platform enhancements and overall functionality. Collaborate with districts to implement comprehensive career development activities to support ICAPs. Collaborate on a regular basis with DESE School Counseling staff to ensure regional and state career education initiatives are aligned. Facilitate career planning opportunities such as regional STEAM events and career fairs in collaboration with Missouri Career Pathway Regional Consultants. MEETING/CONFERENCE ACTIVITIES Career Advisors will: Attend and participate in conferences and workshops related to career education and workforce development as approved by DESE School Counseling staff, ensuring any conference participation or presentations receive prior approval. Attend DESE required RCA meetings. Attend Missouri Connections state trainer required meetings. REQUIRED TRAVEL RCAs are expected to travel within their assigned RPDC region to provide Missouri Connections support, school visits, and regional training. Attendance at DESE-required meetings/conferences may also require statewide travel. Other duties assigned Typical Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in the following field's of study: education, education administration, education counseling, or appropriate related field required. Master's degree in the following field's of study: educational leadership, career education and workforce development, counseling is preferred. Experience: Ten (10) years of experience in education, with an emphasis on career readiness and workforce development required. Core knowledge of career education, Individual Career and Academic Plans (ICAPs), and Missouri Connections. Experience in planning, coordinating, and facilitating student-centered events, with the ability to manage logistics and engage stakeholders. Experience with group facilitation, presentation and adult learning Licenses and Certifications Valid teaching and/or administrators certificate. Valid driver’s license. Special Instructions: Full-time staff & 12-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks paid vacation per year; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. 9-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. Part-time benefits-eligible positions: Benefits include generous education assistance for the employee. Temporary, adjunct, student employment, or graduate assistant positions: Benefits are not included. Completed UCM online application for employment required. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A review will begin immediately and continue until filled unless indicated otherwise. NOTE: A background check is required for the selected candidate of all staff, faculty, adjunct, and temporary positions and any job offer is contingent on the results of this check. Student employees and graduate assistants do not require a background check to be conducted prior to employment. The University of Central Missouri is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our faculty and staff are the university’s most valuable asset, and our goal is to provide a robust Total Rewards Program designed to help them maintain a happy, healthy, and productive lifestyle. Highlights from UCM's total rewards package for full-time employees include: 32% (staff) and 6% (faculty) defined retirement contribution, paid by the university; Voluntary Tax-Sheltered Annuity (TSA) programs (403(b) and 457(b)) that allow eligible employees to make additional pre-tax contributions to a retirement plan; Employees can earn up to full tuition (15 credit hours) for themselves per academic year. Full-time employees are also eligible for up to $175 towards non-credit courses each fiscal year. Employees can earn up to full tuition for their dependents; Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans that begin on the first of the month following your date of hire. Basic dental and vision insurance paid at 100% by the university; Available Health and Dependent Flexible Spending Accounts; University-paid basic life insurance (including accidental death and dismemberment) and short-term and long-term disability insurance coverage; Generous leave accruals that begin accruing on your start date, plus 14 paid holidays per year. The UCM Childcare Center on the Warrensburg campus can provide faculty, staff, and students quality care for their children ages six weeks to 10 years. The Student Recreation and Wellness Center (SRWC) is free for all employees and is located on the Warrensburg campus. An Employee Assistance Program is available to all employees and their immediate family members to help assist with personal challenges you may face in your daily life; UCM offers an Employee Discount Program through Working Advantage. To learn more about the wonderful benefits available as a University of Central Missouri employee, visit our benefits page ! Employer University of Central Missouri (UCM) Address PO Box 800 Warrensburg, Missouri, 64093-5299 Phone (660) 543-4255 Website https://www.ucmo.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email UCM Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your na