      "description": "UCM Career Opportunities | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Nurse Practitioner Part Time | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Nurse Practitioner Part Time | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. UCM Career Opportunities Menu UCM Career Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Nurse Practitioner Part Time Print Apply ﻿ Nurse Practitioner Part Time Salary $55.00 Hourly Location UCMO - Warrensburg, MO Job Type Non-Exempt Staff Part Time Job Number 997088 Division Campus Community Health Fee Opening Date 07/24/2026 Description Benefits Questions Description Provides professional nursing care to clients of University Health Center in an advanced practice role consistent with the Missouri Nurse Practice Act and the Code of State Regulations-General Rules governing Advanced Practice Nursing in the State of Missouri. Delivers primary, acute, preventive, sexual, and reproductive health care services in a college health setting. Services include assessment, diagnosis, treatment, prescribing, health education, contraception counseling, family planning, sexually transmitted infection testing and treatment, pregnancy testing and options counseling, and appropriate follow-up or referral as indicated. Ensures that care is provided in a confidential, supportive, inclusive, culturally responsive, and nonjudgmental manner. Serves as clinical preceptor for Advanced Practice Nurses as requested. Serves as a member of the clinical leadership team, performing administrative duties as requested. Examples of Duties Delivers Advanced Practice Clinical Care in a College Health Setting - 90% Provides professional nursing care to clients of University Health Center in an advanced practice role consistent with The Missouri Nurse Practice Act and the Code of State Regulations-General Rules governing Advanced Practice Nursing, in the State of Missouri. Clinical Education and Leadership Support - 10% Typical Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in nursing required. Master’s degree in Nursing, Family Nurse Practitioner required. Experience: Two (2) years of experience in general nursing practice preferred, which may be concurrent with ambulatory care experience. One (1) year of experience in an ambulatory care setting in an advanced practice role is preferred. Experience in college health, urgent care, primary care, women’s health, adolescent/young adult health, or public health preferred. Supplemental Information Physical/Environmental Factors: Possible exposure to infectious and communicable diseases. This is a part time position working 32 hours per week during Fall and Spring semesters and limited but as needed hours during the Summer semester.   This position does not work when students are not on campus. Special Instructions: Full-time staff & 12-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks paid vacation per year; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. 9-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. Part-time benefits-eligible positions: Benefits include generous education assistance for the employee. Temporary, adjunct, student employment, or graduate assistant positions: Benefits are not included. Completed UCM online application for employment required. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A review will begin immediately and continue until filled unless indicated otherwise. NOTE: A background check is required for the selected candidate of all staff, faculty, adjunct, and temporary positions and any job offer is contingent on the results of this check. Student employees and graduate assistants do not require a background check to be conducted prior to employment. The University of Central Missouri is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our faculty and staff are the university’s most valuable asset, and our goal is to provide a robust Total Rewards Program designed to help them maintain a happy, healthy, and productive lifestyle. Highlights from UCM's total rewards package for full-time employees include: 32% (staff) and 6% (faculty) defined retirement contribution, paid 100% by the university; Voluntary Tax-Sheltered Annuity (TSA) programs (403(b) and 457(b)) that allow eligible employees to make additional pre-tax contributions to a retirement plan; Employees can earn up to 6 credit hours for themselves per academic year. Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans that begin on the first of the month following your date of hire. Basic dental and vision insurance paid at 100% by the university; Available Health and Dependent Flexible Spending Accounts; University-paid basic life insurance (including accidental death and dismemberment) and short-term and long-term disability insurance coverage; Generous leave accruals that begin accruing on your start date, plus 14 paid holidays per year. The UCM Childcare Center on the Warrensburg campus can provide faculty, staff, and students quality care for their children ages six weeks to 10 years. The Student Recreation and Wellness Center (SRWC) is free for all employees and is located on the Warrensburg campus. An Employee Assistance Program is available to all employees and their immediate family members to help assist with personal challenges you may face in your daily life; UCM offers an Employee Discount Program through Working Advantage. To learn more about the wonderful benefits available as a University of Central Missouri employee, visit our benefits page ! 01 Do you understand that this position will be working 32 hours per week during Fall and Spring semesters and limited hours during the summer as needed?   This position will not be working when students are not on campus. Yes No Required Question Employer University of Central Missouri (UCM) Address PO Box 800 Warrensburg, Missouri, 64093-5299 Phone (660) 543-4255 Website https://www.ucmo.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email UCM Ca