      "title": "UCM Career Opportunities",
      "description": "UCM Career Opportunities | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Network Analyst II | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Network Analyst II | University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. UCM Career Opportunities Menu UCM Career Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Network Analyst II Print Apply ﻿ Network Analyst II Salary $59,560.00 Annually Location UCMO - Warrensburg, MO Job Type Exempt Staff Full Time Job Number 999345 Division Infrastructure Services Opening Date 03/11/2026 Description Benefits Questions Description Installs, maintains, documents and supports network, unified communications, and academic/administrative classroom/meeting room interactive presentation systems and infrastructure equipment. Conducts research, testing, and evaluation of new and proposed infrastructure technologies in support of the campus-wide Ethernet LAN/WAN infrastructure, related unified communications infrastructure technologies, and related classroom/meeting room interactive presentation systems and technologies. Communicates network, system-wide, and customer-specific related information to Office of Technology departments, the campus community, and specific customers. Ensures that the 2000 node UCM unified communication infrastructure, the 25,000 node campus-wide wired Ethernet infrastructure, the 400 classroom/meeting room presentation system and technologies, and the campus-wide wireless infrastructure footprint of approximately 4 million square feet functions properly. Lead efforts and manage network technologies pertaining to the university Ethernet switching, routing, and Wi-Fi infrastructure. Additionally lead and manage technologies deployed within and in support of audio/video collaboration and presentation technologies within the university classroom, conference, and meeting rooms across campus building/facilitates. Assist with providing vision, leadership, and direction in the development, management, and evaluation of all university teaching and learning technology services and technologies that support teaching, learning and business needs. Assist with providing leadership and assistance in technology procedure development and implementation, project management, and planning and administration. Assist with the development, definition and communicate an instructional/learning technology services. Assists with the direction, health, and ongoing operational aspects of the campus-wide unified communication VOIP infrastructure. Examples of Duties 30% Plans installations by studying customer orders, plans, manuals, and technical specifications; ordering and gathering equipment, supplies, materials, and tools, assessing installation site; preparing and installation diagram. 30% Install, maintain, and troubleshoot infrastructure hardware and software; including but not limited to operating systems, network applications, and application suites; upgrade/update infrastructure server hardware and software. Install, maintain and troubleshoot network hardware and connections, including but not limited to inter/intra building communications, routers, switches, patch cables, file server hardware, classroom and meeting room video projection equipment, etc. 30% Install and provide maintenance/support for hardware and software utilized in IP communications infrastructures which adhere to TCP /IP and Internet standards such as layer 3 routing protocols ( OSPP , BGP , MSDP and the like), DNS resolution troubleshooting as related to the transport and understanding of DHCP basic communication functionality, video and audio transport troubleshooting and installations ( HDMI , VGA , IP, and USB connectivity troubleshooting), etc. Perform appropriate backup and health monitoring of infrastructure routers, switches, video/audio presentation equipment, unified communications equipment, and associated file servers and their configurations. Provide information to faculty, staff, and students regarding new systems or system changes that will impact how members of the Central computing community utilize network resources. Provide technical instruction/demonstration and training for User Services staff concerning system and network changes, including but not limited to clients, servers, file server, and network configurations. 10% Create, configure, troubleshoot and update documentation on network systems and infrastructure components. Typical Qualifications Education : Bachelor’s degree: business, technology, educational technology, instructional technology, or related field required. Mater’s degree preferred – substitution is allowed for Master’s degree. Education may be substituted for experience or if experience may be substituted for education. Note that equivalencies are based on the following: AA or 60 credit hours = 2 years experience; BA/BS or 120 credit hours = 4 years experience; MA/MS = 6 years experience; PhD = 8 years experience. Experience: Three years experience installing, documenting, maintaining, and supporting analog and digital telephone communication endpoints, unified IP telephone communication endpoints, or video/audio including cable maintenance related activities required. Three years experience call center or related direct interactive customer services activities required. Demonstrated job history of increased autonomy to complete job related tasks and processes required. Three years experience installing, maintaining, documenting, and supporting telephone systems, network infrastructures, and/or classroom video/audio presentation environments of more than 500 users, experience with Cisco Systems, Cresstron, Nortel/Avaya, AMX , Poloycom or related manufactures and technologies strongly preferred. Supplemental Information The anticipated start date for this position is no sooner than Friday, May 1st, 2026. Special Instructions: Full-time staff & 12-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks paid vacation per year; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. 9-month faculty benefits-eligible position: Benefits include competitive salary; health, dental, vision, life insurance, AD & D, long-term disability; 3 weeks of accrued sick leave per year; 13 paid holidays; retirement; and generous education assistance for an employee, spouse and dependent children taking classes at UCM. Part-time benefits-eligible positions: Benefits include generous education assistance for the employee. Temporary, adjunct, student employment, or graduate assistant positions: Benefits are not included. Completed UCM online application for employment required. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A review will begin immediately and continue until filled unless indicated otherwise. NOTE: A background check is required for the selected candidate of all staff, faculty, adjunct, and temporary positions and any job offer is contingent on the results of this check. Student employees and graduate assistants do not require a background check to be conducted prior to employment. The University of Central Missouri is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our faculty and staff are the university’s most valuable asset, and our goal is to provide a robust Total Rewards Program designed to help them maintain a happy, healthy, and productive lifestyle. Highlights from UCM's total rewards package for full-time employees include: 32% (staff) and 6% (faculty) defined retirement contribution, paid by the university; Voluntary Tax-Sheltered Annuity (TSA) programs (403(b) and 457(b)) that allow eligible employees to make additional pre-tax contributions to a retirement plan; Employees can earn up to full tuition (15 credit hours) for themselves per academic year. Full-time employees are also eligible for up to $175 towards non-credit courses each fiscal year. Employees can earn up to full tuition for their dependents; Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans that begin on the first of the month following your date of hire. Basic dental and vision insurance paid at 100% by the university; Available Health and Dependent Flexible Spending Accounts; University-paid basic life insurance (including accidental death and dismemberment) and short-term and long-term disability insurance coverage; Generous leave accruals that begin accruing on your start date, plus 14 paid holidays per year. The UCM Childcare Center on the Warrensburg campus can provide faculty, staff, and students quality care for their children ages six weeks to 10 years. The Student Recreation and Wellness Center (SRWC) is free for all employees and is located on the Warrensburg campus. An Employee Assistance Program is available to all employees and their immediate family members to help assist with personal challenges you may face in your daily life; UCM offers an Employee Discount Program through Working Advantage. To learn more about the wonderful benefits available as a University of Central Missouri employee, visit our benefits page ! 01 Do you have a Bachelor's degree or higher in the field of business, technology, educational technology, instructional technology or a closely related field? Yes No 02 How many years of experience installing, documenting, maintaining, or supporting analog and digital telephone communication endpoints, unified IP telephone communication endpoints, or video/audio including cable maintenance related activities experience do you currently have? Less than 1 year of experience. More than 1 year, but less than 2 years of experience. More than 2 years, but less than 3 years of experience. More than 3 years, but less than 4 years of experience. More than 4 years, but less than 5 years of experience. More than 5 years of experience. 03 How many years of  call center or related direct interactive customer services activities experience do you currently have? Less than 1 year of experience. More than 1 year, but less than 2 years of experience. More than 2 years, but less than 3 years of experience. More than 3 years, but less than 4 years of experience. More than 4 years, but less than 5 years of experience. More than 5 years of experience. 04 I understand that, as a condition of employment for this position, I am required to complete a criminal background check and obtain Criminal Justice Information Security (CJIS) clearance, which includes a fingerprint-based criminal history check. Yes, I understand that, prior to being offered this position, I am required to successfully obtain Criminal Justice Information Security (CJIS) clearance through a fingerprint-based criminal history check, in addition to completing a criminal background check. 05 This role requires full-time, on-site work at our Warrensburg, Missouri campus and is not eligible for full-time remote work. Are you able to work on-site in Warrensburg, Missouri each day? Yes, I am able to work on-site in Warrensburg, Missouri each day, as required, and understand that this role requires full-time, on-campus presence. This position is not a remote position. No, I am looking for a remote position, and I am unable to report to on-site work in Warrensburg, Missouri, each day, as expected. Required Question Employer University of Central Missouri (UCM) Address PO Box 800 Warrensburg, Missouri, 64093-5299 Phone (660) 543-4255 Website https://www.ucmo.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email UCM Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities UCM Career Opportunities Menu Close Menu University of Central Missouri Career Opportunities UCM Ca